	tags: general,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function visually displays the maze&#x27;s current state, including the player&#x27;s position, walls, exit, and objects (if the player hasn't collected them yet).
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>maze</pf> (struct) number — : The structure representing the maze. It includes all the fields described in <pf>HW4_initialize_game</pf>.</p>
			<p><pf>player</pf> (struct) number — - The structure representing the player's current state. It includes all the fields described in <pf>HW4_initialize_game</pf></p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>fprintf</pf> number — This function has no explicit return values. Its primary purpose is to clear the console and display the maze's current state using <pf>fprintf</pf>.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>This function must consider the player's line of sight. If the player cannot "see" a wall or object, it should be displayed using the "dark" icon.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This function does not display the inventory items, only the maze.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
